{title: I Have Overcome}
{subtitle: John 16:33}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Now we know [Bb]that you know everything
[Eb]No one needs to question you
Because of this we believe
[Gm]You came from [F]God today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Bb]Do you believe now I ask you
[Eb]The hour is coming soon
It has al[Gm]ready come to us
When [F]you will be scattered
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]In me you may have peace
[Eb]In the world you will have trouble
But [Gm]take heart my [F]soul
I have overcome the [Eb]world
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Each to his own home you go
[Eb]You will leave me alone
Yet [Gm]I am not alone friend
[F]For the Father is with [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]I have told you these [F]things
So that in [Bb]me you may have [Eb]peace
[Cm7]Look up and [F]find rest
In the [Eb]truth [F]I hold [Bb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In me you may have peace
[Eb]In the world you will have trouble
But [Gm]take heart my [F]soul
I have overcome the [Eb]world
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Take [Gm]heart and stand [F]firm
I have over[Bb]come
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
